Do not take an argument of a structural call for a value class without a class

A structural call through `reflectiveSelectable`, or any `Selectable`, whose
argument has a type with no class symbol crashed the compiler:

    java.lang.ClassCastException: NoSymbol cannot be cast to ClassSymbol
      at dotty.tools.dotc.typer.Dynamic.handleRepeated

scala/scala3 #17564 unboxes value-class arguments of a dynamic call, and
finds the argument's class with `classSymbol.asClass`. An opaque alias
bounded by an intersection of unrelated classes, as Soundness's `Text` is
(`opaque type Text <: Matchable & caps.Pure`), has none. Such an argument is
no value class, and is now passed as it is.

Found in Soundness's enigmatic, whose providers are reached through
structural refinements.

